{"html":"<div>\n<p>Learn how to connect your OneLaser XT or XRF to LightBurn via USB. Follow this simple setup guide to install LightBurn, configure Ruida, set origin, and start engraving.</p><div>\n\n</div><figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-usb-cable/connect-lightburn-via-usb-cable.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"USB connection setup for OneLaser XT and XRF machines\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><h2 id=\"operational-guide\"> Operational Guide</h2><div>\n\n</div><p>1. Install the LightBurn software, please see the link below to install:</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://docs.lightburnsoftware.com/latest/GetStarted/InstallLightBurn/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Install the LightBurn software</a></p><div>\n\n</div><p>2. Connect your computer and laser machine with a USB cable.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-usb-cable/connect-lightburn-via-usb-cable_2.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Plugging USB cable into OneLaser machine\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>3. Open LightBurn and set a connection.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-usb-cable/connect-lightburn-via-usb-cable_3.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Opening LightBurn software to create device connection\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>4. Select Ruida.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-usb-cable/connect-lightburn-via-usb-cable_4.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Selecting Ruida controller in LightBurn\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>5. Select Serial/USB.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-usb-cable/connect-lightburn-via-usb-cable_5.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Choosing Serial USB connection option in LightBurn\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>6. Name your laser and enter the work area — for X Series, the area is 600 × 300 mm.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-usb-cable/connect-lightburn-via-usb-cable_6.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Entering device name and work area size for OneLaser X Series\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>7. Set the Rear Left as Origin.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-usb-cable/connect-lightburn-via-usb-cable_7.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Setting rear left origin position in LightBurn\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>8. Then it&#x27;s finish.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-usb-cable/connect-lightburn-via-usb-cable_8.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"LightBurn device setup completion screen\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>9. Back to the home page and select XT. If it shows “Ready,” it means the software is connected.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-usb-cable/connect-lightburn-via-usb-cable_9.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"LightBurn showing OneLaser XT device ready status\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div></div>","toc":[{"id":"operational-guide","level":2,"text":"Operational Guide"}]}